{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/config.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T15:58:58.925377Z","id":"6011cecd1752156802dacadc92021f4cdb331a0735a154c7d2498418156e9151","body":{"detail":"Spec 2026-10-27-sizzle-reel-design §9.3 says config.ts refuses a full reel outside 60–80 s and a short cut outside 40–50 s. While web/reel/reel.toml lists only some vignettes (one, realtime, today: 12.2 s in full), parseReel cannot apply that check, so it lives in checkCuts, which config.test.ts exercises but no recorder or composer calls. The composition (`//web/reel:reel`, phase 2) should call it once reel.toml lists every vignette of spec §3.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":180},"end":{"line":182},"content_hash":"cfb0132daace495a1f72d9ef133ac081a4b32163497cf9da3e9d4d621e26f664"},"suggested_fix":"Call checkCuts from the composition's entry point (and the composer's own reel.toml check) when reel.toml names all nine vignettes.","summary":"Nothing calls checkCuts yet: parseReel does not hold reel.toml to the 60–80 s full and 40–50 s short cuts","tags":["session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/reel.bzl","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T15:58:58.925763Z","id":"b1cb9ebc6897ab71a4bc79acdc82c77bd4a01a12f174a92a500dddc506edb6b6","body":{"detail":"The recorder imports only web/e2e/fixtures.ts, time.ts and hosted-helpers.ts and reads web/package.json, but //web:files is the whole web project (shell, bridge, unit tests, every e2e spec). Spec §8 lists the e2e helpers it imports as the input. A recording takes tens of seconds per vignette, and only `just reel` pays it, but a test edit invalidating every <id>_fast and later <id>_frames is wasted work. A narrower input needs web/BUILD.bazel to split the e2e helpers out of :files_tests (two copy_to_bin of one file conflict).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":50},"end":{"line":55},"content_hash":"c3c695679dc521554c2b9c5bfeaeb100d62971cc664d1bdbf9fe4164b434b7f0"},"suggested_fix":"In web/BUILD.bazel, a copy_to_bin of web/e2e/*.ts minus *.spec.ts (taken out of :files_tests' glob) plus package.json, and the reel's srcs name that instead of //web:files.","summary":"Every recording reads all of //web:files, so an edit to any web unit or browser test re-records every vignette","tags":["session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/record.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T15:58:58.926Z","id":"a5b80597b38f3d77c84a282bbe5b7c03be9607b762543a58ae3ee59db7848e51","body":{"detail":"hostedDaemon in web/e2e/hosted-helpers.ts calls test.skip when the daemon takes another port, which only works inside a Playwright test, so the recorder restates its [hosted] config (public_origin, setup_secret_env) and fails instead. Factoring a startHosted() that both call would keep one copy of that config, at the cost of touching the e2e helpers (and so rerunning every browser test) in the reel's first change.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":106},"end":{"line":113},"content_hash":"e84d9b83eb5558019b168d93b6a16079470631fecf0c695eeadd665dedb50911"},"summary":"Factor a test-free hosted daemon start out of web/e2e/hosted-helpers.ts instead of restating its config here","tags":["revisit:the [hosted] config hostedDaemon writes changes, or a second recorder needs it","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/record.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T15:58:58.926251Z","id":"e373ab8bb26916a77a551a363ff8bf15eb0fb7a493db0131c7fb0acb29b1f7e5","body":{"detail":"Playwright's recordVideo scales a page's screencast down to fit the size it is given, never up: at size 1600 × 1000 a 1280 × 800 viewport at device scale 1.25 recorded as 1280 × 800 in the top left corner of a grey 1600 × 1000 frame. So fast mode records at the viewport's size; the capture's 1600 × 1000 device pixels (spec §5) come from deterministic mode (CDP screenshots). A reel composed from fast clips (`reel_fast`, spec §8) must scale them up or frame them smaller.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":126},"end":{"line":129},"content_hash":"f23a5ef1a46edaf27ef06dbcec997c8ae87cd341ce7c388121c513fbf4b4a81f"},"summary":"The fast clip is 1280 × 800 (the viewport's CSS size), not the capture's 1600 × 1000","tags":["session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
